{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{x^2-x+5}{4x-1}$ is a rational expression.\n\nTo find the derivative of rational expressions, we use **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x^2-x+5}{4x-1}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(4x-1)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2-x+5)-(x^2-x+5)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(4x-1)}{(4x-1)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(4x-1)(2x-1)-(x^2-x+5)(4)}{(4x-1)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }(x^2-x+5)\\text{ \u0026 }(4x-1)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{8x^2-4x-2x+1-4x^2+4x-20}{(4x-1)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Expand}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{4x^2-2x-19}{(4x-1)^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x^2-x+5}{4x-1}\\right)=\\dfrac{4x^2-2x-19}{(4x-1)^2}$, or any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x^2-x+5}{4x-1}\\right)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{4x^2-2x-19}{\\left(4x-1\\right)^2}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
